Write me a letter, send it by name

180
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Email, that is folks.

181
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:06,000
And here's an answer to one of your emails.

182
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:17,000
So a couple of quick questions that came into the email inbox this week.

183
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Stephen Jensen says this: our troop is mostly a car camping troop,

184
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:25,000
But we're broadening our horizons a bit into backpacking.

185
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:29,000
I have lots of excited scouts and nervous parents.

186
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Yep, okay, understood.

187
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:38,000
He said it came to my attention that one of my new scouts has a pretty severe asthma problem

188
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
And he could need a nebulizer if it gets bad.

189
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:45,000
This hike, although short, will be at a high altitude.

190
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
What's your experience with asthmatic boys?

191
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,000
I know this is something that seems to be getting more prevalent.

192
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,000
How would you handle it?

193
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Thanks, Clark.

194
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Always an amazing podcast, truly a work of public service,

195
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Stephen Jensen. well, thank you, Stephen, for the kind words.

196
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,000
You know what. this is pretty easy,

197
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:06,000
And I would say that this advice applies to any medical condition.

198
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:09,000
You always go to the parents and the doctor

199
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Describing the trip and the likely conditions

200
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:15,000
And then you ask for their approval.

201
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
You're not a professional

202
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:20,000
And neither are the parents really.

203
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:24,000
So if there's a substantial doubt about something like that,

204
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:28,000
You want to find out and you want to find out authoritatively

205
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:31,000
From somebody who is a professional, who's a doctor,

206
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Who knows about such things, whether or not this is advisable.

207
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Now you talk about at altitude.

208
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:43,000
Well, altitude concerns really only start to kick in around 7,000 feet.

209
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:48,000
You definitely need to be concerned about the way everybody is going to react

210
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,000
And not just somebody with asthma.

211
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:55,000
You definitely want to familiarize yourself with hiking at altitude.

212
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:58,000
Like I said, from my experience and my knowledge,

213
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:02,000
7,000 feet is kind of the point where you need to be concerned.

214
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Not a lot of concerns for us here out east

215
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Because we don't have too many places that are 7,000 feet above sea level.

216
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:14,000
So the other thing I'd add just for good measure

217
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Is that a short hike and easy going

218
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:21,000
And all the other elements set up for easy success

219
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Is really important to anybody going on their first backpacking trip.

220
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
You don't want them to endure an ordeal.

221
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:31,000
You want them to have a really good time and be ready to go out and do more.

222
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:34,000
So thanks, Stephen, again for being in touch.

223
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
I had this note from Tom Brewer

224
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Said. I just wanted to repeat what I've already said.

225
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,000
I'm still enjoying and learning from the podcast.

226
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Keep up the good work.

227
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,000
And Tom is way up there in Canada

228
