230
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,000
I've got one that can barely put up a tent.

231
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Do you screen for that?

232
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Do you train them yourself?

233
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,000
I mean, how do you manage this?

234
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Well, there's a couple different ways to do that.

235
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:02,000
First of all, getting that outdoor training for scout leaders.

236
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,000
That's always important.

237
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,000
The other thing is

238
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Is that when there are instruction times for scouts,

239
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:13,000
You want to grab that new volunteer adult by the elbow

240
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:16,000
And say: this is something that you need to know.

241
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:19,000
So you need to pay very close attention to what's going on here

242
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:23,000
And let him be trained right along with the scouts,

243
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Although I like older scouts to be the instructors

244
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,000
For the majority of the time.

245
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Every once in a while, when you have somebody who's very new,

246
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:36,000
You might want them to instruct the skill that they need to learn.

247
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
That's a little counterintuitive,

248
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
But sometimes it works very well

249
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Because usually adults that volunteer for scouting,

250
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
They have a desire to help out

251
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:50,000
And to teach and instruct different skills.

252
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:54,000
And so, scout handbook,

253
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Here you go.

254
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,000
New volunteer next week

255
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:01,000
I would like you to instruct the scouts on putting up tents,

256
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,000
Choosing campsites.

257
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
And when they look at you and they say

258
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,000
I know nothing about that,

259
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Say hey, it's all in the scout handbook.

260
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Stay 15 minutes ahead of the scouts

261
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
And you'll be in good shape.

262
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:15,000
But that has worked.

263
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,000
That has worked as well.

264
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:20,000
We have a first-year camper program at our summer camp

265
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:24,000
That goes through a lot of those very basic scout skills

266
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
In a week's time

267
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:31,000
And sending a new volunteer to help

268
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:34,000
With that particular thing

269
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Can also be a real eye-opener for them.

270
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:39,000
So there's direct and indirect approaches to that

271
